📌 File & Folder Explanation (Simple)

Run this to start everything.

📊 dashboard.py

➡️ The visual dashboard that shows:

Sentiment charts

Trends

Mood changes

➕ add_data_vector_db.py

➡️ Stores data in a vector database for fast searching.

📈 review_sentiment_trend_spike.py

➡️ Detects sudden emotional spikes (anger, happiness, trending topics).

🧪 data_analysis/ Folder


File	Purpose
cleaning.py	Cleans messy data
sentiment.py	Detects happy/sad emotions
topic_modeling_2.py	Finds topics like tech, food, movies
category.py	Categorizes data
reduce_data.py	Reduces large data
merged_data.py	Combines multiple datasets

🌍 external_api/ Folder

This folder collects real-world data from the internet

reddit_api.py → Reddit posts

news.py → News articles

rapid_api.py → Reviews from websites

sentiment_news_spike.py → Detects emotional news spikes

sentiment_reddit_spike.py → Detects Reddit sentiment spikes

🔔 notification/notification.py

➡️ Sends alerts when something important happens.

📁 final_data/

➡️ Stores cleaned and final datasets in CSV/Excel format.

🧠 consumer_sentiment_faiss/

➡️ A FAISS vector database for fast sentiment search.

⚙️ requirements.txt

➡️ List of Python libraries needed to run the project.

🔐 .env

➡️ Stores secret API keys 

🚀 How to Run the Project
1️⃣ Install Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

2️⃣ Run the Project
streamlit run dashboard.py

api files 

1. news_api.py
2. reddit.py 
3. rapid.py